          "guid": "ms2xvy8jbolewj3h",
          "message": {
            "text": "The expected-PNG cache silently invalidated this whole mode's first measurement, and the cache token (0) is what fixes it — this is the sharpest edge in the change.\n\nThe cached artifact is a screenshot taken by the CAPTURE browser. A capture-side Chromium flag changes that screenshot and nothing else in the key (source HTML, viewport, Playwright version, capture-script hash, capture-node hash), so a flagged run happily reuses the unflagged PNG and reports numbers for a condition it never ran.\n\nThat is not hypothetical: the first three-condition run during this ticket produced coverage identical to four decimal places across default / symmetric / asymmetric, which is what prompted looking at the key at all. It is also the exact failure this mode exists to prevent, reproduced one layer down — the mode is for measuring honestly, and it was itself measuring a cache.\n\nTwo properties to preserve if this is ever touched: the token must be empty when no capture flags are set (otherwise every default run re-captures and every committed cache entry is discarded), and it must exclude the raster flags (those affect actual.png, which is never cached — including them would fragment the cache for no reason).\n\nVerified after the fix by watching the cache split (27 → 38 entries when a new capture-flag condition was introduced) and by the three-condition tables in the attached artifact.\n",
            "markdown": "The expected-PNG cache silently invalidated this whole mode's first measurement, and the [cache token](0) is what fixes it — this is the sharpest edge in the change.\n\nThe cached artifact is a screenshot taken by the CAPTURE browser. A capture-side Chromium flag changes that screenshot and nothing else in the key (source HTML, viewport, Playwright version, capture-script hash, capture-node hash), so a flagged run happily reuses the unflagged PNG and reports numbers for a condition it never ran.\n\nThat is not hypothetical: the first three-condition run during this ticket produced coverage **identical to four decimal places** across default / symmetric / asymmetric, which is what prompted looking at the key at all. It is also the exact failure this mode exists to prevent, reproduced one layer down — the mode is for measuring honestly, and it was itself measuring a cache.\n\nTwo properties to preserve if this is ever touched: the token must be **empty** when no capture flags are set (otherwise every default run re-captures and every committed cache entry is discarded), and it must **exclude** the raster flags (those affect `actual.png`, which is never cached — including them would fragment the cache for no reason).\n\nVerified after the fix by watching the cache split (27 → 38 entries when a new capture-flag condition was introduced) and by the three-condition tables in the attached artifact.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tests/html-test-suite.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 116,
                  "endLine": 128,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "// DM-1790: and fold the CAPTURE browser's Chromium flags in too. The cached\n// artifact is a screenshot taken by that browser, so a capture-side flag\n// changes it while changing nothing else in the key — a flagged run would\n// otherwise reuse the unflagged PNG and report numbers for a condition it never\n// ran. Empty (and so key-neutral) unless `DOMOTION_CAPTURE_FLAGS` is set.\nfunction expectedCacheKey(htmlBytes: Buffer, fixtureHeight: number): string {\n  return createHash(\"sha256\")\n    .update(htmlBytes)\n    .update(`|${WIDTH}x${fixtureHeight}@${CAPTURE_DPR}x|${PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION}|${CAPTURE_SCRIPT_HASH}|${CAPTURE_NODE_HASH}${captureFlagsCacheToken()}`)\n    .digest(\"hex\");\n}\nfunction expectedCachePngPath(key: string): string { return resolve(EXPECTED_CACHE_DIR, `${key}.png`); }\nfunction expectedCacheMetaPath(key: string): string { return resolve(EXPECTED_CACHE_DIR, `${key}.json`); }"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "risk"
            ]
          },
